the tool's own PID) so the production path is not wholly untested.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1722,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC6: 'process-inspection seam is injectable so the test never depends on real system process state'","AC5 flags 'a bounded decoy process it is given' (injected, not real)"],"finding":"The check's real process-inspection adapter (parsing live ps/PID-1 state) is never exercised end-to-end; every AC exercises only the injected seam, so the production listing path could be broken and all checks still pass.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2f9d422ce0ee67f1","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC6; Testing","norm_id":"ne886ef55898fce6a","priority":0.7778,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The real ps-parsing adapter has a bug (wrong column, PPID parse); tests are green because they only feed synthetic process records"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Keep the injectable seam for the unit tests, but add one AC or a documented rationale asserting the default (non-injected) adapter runs against the live process table without error, e.g. running the check on the host returns exit 0 and structured output.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the guidance ACs with AGENTS.md's stated leanness/pointer convention: state whether the bounded pattern, teardown trap, why-line, orphan-reaping rule, and operator reclamation note are inlined in AGENTS.md or placed in a docs/ page with a one-line AGENTS.md pointer, and target the AC literal-presence checks accordingly.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.164,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AGENTS.md lines 10-12: 'Keep this file lean: an @-import loads at launch and does not reduce context, so already-documented topics are one-line pointers into docs/, not restated sections.'","AC #2 requires 'a copy-pasteable bounded pattern (for example `timeout 120 python -c '...'` &)' and 'a process-group teardown (`trap 'kill 0' EXIT INT TERM`), with one line on why an unbounded loop outlives harness death' — verbatim literals asserted to appear in AGENTS.md.","DoD: 'A short operator note on reclaiming an already-leaked batch' also targets the canonical file.","ABSENCE: the plan never states whether the detailed pattern/teardown/reclamation content should live in a docs/ page with a one-line AGENTS.md pointer (the file's convention) or be inlined, leaving the executor to guess."],"finding":"The guidance ACs (#1, #2, #3, and the DoD operator note) require embedding multi-line copy-pasteable literals and prose directly in AGENTS.md, but AGENTS.md's own stated policy is to stay lean and point to docs/ rather than restating multi-line sections. The plan does not reconcile where the full pattern/teardown/reclamation content lives versus a one-line pointer, creating an instruction-locality conflict on the very file being edited.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f384eb25b94cc5638","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria #1/#2/#3 and Definition of Done (operator note); target file AGENTS.md","norm_id":"na883d57d1eeba5f8","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor inlines several paragraphs plus code blocks into AGENTS.md and trips the file's leanness convention, or a reviewer rejects the placement.","The verification-by-literal ACs force inlining into AGENTS.md even though the file's policy would put the body in docs/ with a pointer."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Put the full bounded-pattern/teardown/reclamation body in a docs/ page (e.g. a subagent-resource-hygiene doc) and require AGENTS.md to carry only a lean one-line pointer plus the load-bearing rule; retarget AC #2/#4 literal checks and the DoD operator note to that docs/ file, keeping the AGENTS.md-presence check limited to the pointer and the core prohibition.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["vague/subjective terms present: sufficient"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"[ ] State how/whether the detection check gets invoked automatically (e.g. a login/periodic hook or an operator-runbook step), or explicitly scope out auto-invocation with a rationale, so the 'no sweep exists' gap is actually closed rather than left to memory.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3525,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC: 'runnable on demand as a plain command with no dependency on any CI provider'","Why-it-went-unnoticed: 'No sweep exists for long-lived compute processes with no parent.'","The plan adds a check but no scheduled/hook invocation that would run it automatically; DoD lists only 'implemented and covered by the test'"],"finding":"The detection check is purely on-demand and the guidance is advisory; neither is wired to any recurring trigger or enforcement seam, so recurrence detection still depends on a human remembering to run the check — the exact failure mode the incident exposed (four days undetected).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f07114e9d78d3cf51","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (detection check AC) and Definition of Done","norm_id":"n613ec4251073ccf9","priority":0.2475,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future subagent leaks another orphan batch; because nobody runs check_orphaned_load.py, it again goes undetected for days"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the detection check's platform scope (POSIX-only) OR provide a Windows-equivalent orphan/high-CPU heuristic, so `scripts/check_orphaned_load.py` does not silently report zero on a Windows host where PID-1 reparenting does not exist.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5a","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'A detection check reports compute processes whose parent is PID 1 and whose accumulated CPU time exceeds a threshold ... with no dependency on any CI provider (project.portability)'","Platform fact: Windows has no PID-1 init/orphan-reaper; orphaned processes are not reparented to a stable PID 1 and there is no /proc, so a ppid==1 predicate is meaningless there.","The incident host is macOS (a POSIX platform), and the plan generalizes the check without stating platform scope."],"finding":"The detection check's core predicate — 'parent is PID 1' — encodes a POSIX-only orphan-reaping model. On Windows there is no PID-1 init that adopts orphaned processes, so the predicate never matches and the check silently reports nothing, giving false assurance that no leaked load generators exist. AC4 tags this deliverable `project.portability` but the plan does not state a platform scope or a Windows-equivalent detection.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff704bffb29f5f893","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC4: 'compute processes whose parent is PID 1 and whose accumulated CPU time exceeds a threshold ... (project.portability)'","norm_id":"n4f332db7886cda84","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Platform=Windows developer workstation: an operator runs `python scripts/check_orphaned_load.py`; the ppid==1 predicate matches nothing, the check exits reporting zero orphans even when leaked burners exist, so the leak goes undetected."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add an AC declaring the check POSIX-scoped and documenting that on non-POSIX platforms it emits a clear 'not supported on this platform' notice rather than a silent empty result, or supply a Windows detection path keyed on long-running high-CPU processes without a live parent session.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"low","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_